  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Code that raises exceptions</span>
<span class="kw">try</span>:
    <span class="va">result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">10</span> <span class="op">/</span> <span class="nm">0</span>  <span class="cm"># ZeroDivisionError</span>
<span class="kw">except</span> <span class="nm">ZeroDivisionError</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">"Cannot divide by zero"</span>)

<span class="kw">try</span>:
    <span class="va">x</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">int</span>(<span class="st">"hello"</span>)  <span class="cm"># ValueError</span>
<span class="kw">except</span> <span class="nm">ValueError</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">"Cannot convert to integer"</span>)

<span class="kw">try</span>:
    <span class="kw">with</span> <span class="fn">open</span>(<span class="st">"missing.txt"</span>) <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="va">f</span>:
        <span class="va">data</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">f</span>.<span class="fn">read</span>()
<span class="kw">except</span> <span class="nm">FileNotFoundError</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">"File does not exist"</span>)</code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>What is happening here:</strong> Each try-except catches a specific exception type. If the exception is raised inside the try block, Python jumps to the matching except clause. If no exception occurs, the except block is skipped entirely. Catching specific exceptions (not generic Exception) is professional practice — it tells readers exactly what problems you anticipated.</p>
  </div>

