<!-- ===== SECTION 2: TRY-EXCEPT PATTERNS ===== -->
<section class="section reveal" id="try-except">
  <span class="section-label">Core Concepts</span>
  <h2>Try-Except-Finally Patterns</h2>

  <p>The basic pattern is try code that might fail, except handle specific exceptions, and finally execute cleanup code regardless of success or failure. Understanding these patterns helps you write defensive code that handles edge cases professionally.</p>

  <h3>Multiple Exception Handlers</h3>
  <p>Different exceptions require different responses. Catch them separately to handle each appropriately.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="kw">try</span>:
    <span class="va">num</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">int</span>(<span class="fn">input</span>(<span class="st">"Enter a number: "</span>))
    <span class="va">result</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">100</span> <span class="op">/</span> <span class="va">num</span>
<span class="kw">except</span> <span class="nm">ValueError</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">"Invalid input — not a number"</span>)
<span class="kw">except</span> <span class="nm">ZeroDivisionError</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">"Cannot divide by zero"</span>)
<span class="kw">else</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Success! Result: </span>{<span class="va">result</span>}<span class="st">"</span>)
<span class="kw">finally</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">"Operation complete"</span>)</code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>What is happening here:</strong> Specific exceptions (ValueError, ZeroDivisionError) are caught first with custom messages. The else clause runs only if no exception occurred. Finally runs always — even if there's an uncaught exception — making it perfect for cleanup like closing files or releasing locks.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Finally for Cleanup</h3>
  <p>Resources like open files or network connections must be released even if errors occur. Finally guarantees cleanup code runs.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="cm"># Manual cleanup (error-prone)</span>
<span class="va">f</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">open</span>(<span class="st">"data.txt"</span>, <span class="st">"r"</span>)
<span class="kw">try</span>:
    <span class="va">lines</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">f</span>.<span class="fn">readlines</span>()
<span class="kw">except</span> <span class="nm">IOError</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="va">e</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Cannot read file: </span>{<span class="va">e</span>}<span class="st">"</span>)
<span class="kw">finally</span>:
    <span class="va">f</span>.<span class="fn">close</span>()  <span class="cm"># Guaranteed to run</span>

<span class="cm"># Better: Use context managers (automatic cleanup)</span>
<span class="kw">try</span>:
    <span class="kw">with</span> <span class="fn">open</span>(<span class="st">"data.txt"</span>, <span class="st">"r"</span>) <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="va">f</span>:
        <span class="va">lines</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">f</span>.<span class="fn">readlines</span>()
<span class="kw">except</span> <span class="nm">IOError</span> <span class="kw">as</span> <span class="va">e</span>:
    <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Cannot read file: </span>{<span class="va">e</span>}<span class="st">"</span>)</code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>What is happening here:</strong> The first uses finally to ensure the file closes. The second uses a context manager (with statement), which automatically closes the file. Context managers are preferred because they are cleaner and handle edge cases better. However, understanding finally is crucial for non-context-manager scenarios.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- INFOGRAPHIC: Exception Flow -->
  <div class="infographic reveal">
    <div class="infographic-title">Exception Flow: Try → Except → Finally</div>
    <svg viewBox="0 0 800 280" style="width:100%;max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;display:block">
      <!-- Happy path -->
      <rect x="30" y="20" width="350" height="100" rx="8" fill="rgba(6,255,165,0.08)" stroke="rgba(6,255,165,0.25)"/>
      <text x="50" y="40" fill="#16a34a" font-size="10" font-weight="600">No Exception Raised</text>
      <text x="50" y="60" fill="#7A756B" font-size="9">1. try block executes</text>
      <text x="50" y="78" fill="#7A756B" font-size="9">2. except blocks skipped</text>
      <text x="50" y="96" fill="#7A756B" font-size="9">3. else block runs (if present)</text>
      <text x="50" y="114" fill="#7A756B" font-size="9">4. finally block runs</text>

      <!-- Error path -->
      <rect x="420" y="20" width="350" height="100" rx="8" fill="rgba(255,149,0,0.08)" stroke="rgba(255,149,0,0.25)"/>
      <text x="440" y="40" fill="#C0522F" font-size="10" font-weight="600">Exception Raised</text>
      <text x="440" y="60" fill="#7A756B" font-size="9">1. try block halts</text>
      <text x="440" y="78" fill="#7A756B" font-size="9">2. matching except runs</text>
      <text x="440" y="96" fill="#7A756B" font-size="9">3. else block skipped</text>
      <text x="440" y="114" fill="#7A756B" font-size="9">4. finally block runs</text>

      <!-- Key point -->
      <rect x="30" y="140" width="740" height="120" rx="8" fill="rgba(54,207,201,0.05)" stroke="rgba(54,207,201,0.15)"/>
      <text x="50" y="165" fill="#1A3A6B" font-size="10" font-weight="600">Critical Point:</text>
      <text x="50" y="185" fill="#7A756B" font-size="9">Finally ALWAYS executes, whether exception was caught, re-raised, or if execution completes normally.</text>
      <text x="50" y="205" fill="#7A756B" font-size="9">This makes finally essential for cleanup: closing files, releasing locks, committing transactions.</text>
      <text x="50" y="225" fill="#16a34a" font-size="9" font-weight="600">Best practice: Use context managers (with statement) as they are cleaner and safer.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <!-- KEY TAKEAWAY -->
  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Try code that might fail, except specific exceptions, finally run cleanup</li>
      <li>Use else to run code only if no exception occurred</li>
      <li>Finally guarantees cleanup runs, even with unhandled exceptions</li>
      <li>Prefer context managers (with statement) for automatic resource cleanup</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

