<!-- ===== SECTION 5: PRODUCTION PATTERNS ===== -->
<section class="section reveal" id="production-patterns">
  <span class="section-label">Best Practices</span>
  <h2>Error Handling in Production</h2>

  <p>Production code is different from learning code. Your AI model might run 24/7 processing live data. Network errors happen. Disks fill up. Memory runs out. Professional code doesn't crash — it handles problems gracefully, logs them, and continues safely.</p>

  <h3>Retry Logic with Exponential Backoff</h3>
  <p>Network calls can fail temporarily. Retrying with increasing delays (exponential backoff) often succeeds without user intervention.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="kw">import</span> <span class="nm">time</span>

<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">fetch_with_retry</span>(<span class="va">url</span>, <span class="va">max_retries</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">3</span>):
    <span class="kw">for</span> <span class="va">attempt</span> <span class="kw">in</span> <span class="fn">range</span>(<span class="va">max_retries</span>):
        <span class="kw">try</span>:
            <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="fn">requests</span>.<span class="fn">get</span>(<span class="va">url</span>, <span class="va">timeout</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">5</span>)
        <span class="kw">except</span> <span class="nm">requests</span>.<span class="nm">RequestException</span>:
            <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="va">attempt</span> <span class="op">==</span> <span class="va">max_retries</span> <span class="op">-</span> <span class="nm">1</span>:
                <span class="kw">raise</span>
            <span class="va">wait</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">2</span> <span class="op">**</span> <span class="va">attempt</span>  <span class="cm"># Exponential backoff</span>
            <span class="nm">time</span>.<span class="fn">sleep</span>(<span class="va">wait</span>)</span></code></pre>

  <!-- WHY THIS MATTERS -->
  <div class="why-matters">
    <h4>🌍 Why This Matters</h4>
    <p><strong>In Financial AI:</strong> Transaction processing must handle network failures gracefully. Exponential backoff prevents overwhelming overloaded systems. Custom exceptions for each failure mode (timeout, rate limit, authentication) allow intelligent retrying or alerting.</p>
    <p><strong>In Life Sciences AI:</strong> Data pipelines processing medical records must never lose data or silently corrupt it. Proper exception handling with logging ensures you can audit what went wrong and manually recover if necessary.</p>
  </div>
</section>

